From atkinson at mayo.edu  Mon Apr  1 16:50:23 2002
From: atkinson at mayo.edu (Beth Atkinson)
Date: Mon, 01 Apr 2002 10:50:23 -0600
Subject: New rpart release
Message-ID: <200204011650.g31GoNH29149@aja.mayo.edu>

An update of the rpart routines has been place on
 http://www.mayo.edu/hsr/Sfunc.html  as  "rpart3".

Since the last update (2/2000) there have been some small bug fixes,
and several enhancements.

1. A "cost" argument has been added. 
   This allows the user to weight the variables considered at a split
   point.  For instance, one lab test might be much more expensive than
   another, and we would like it to give at least 10% "better"
   separation before choosing it.  A cost of 1.10 would suitably divide
   the improvement values for that variable.

2. A change to the code for trees that have no splits.  
   Old output: an error message.  New output: a tree (albeit a very small one).

3. The biggest modification was to allow "user written" split rules.
   A set of 3 S-functions (initialize, find split, evaluate node),
   properly packaged, can be given as the `method' argument to
   rpart.  The fit is not as fast as for the built-in rules, but this
   provides an easy way to try out new ideas.  Look at
   test/anovatest.s for an example.

NOTE: The code on the Mayo server is for Splus6/Unix.  Others can
better address Windows and/or R versions.

Beth Atkinson
Terry Therneau

