From a.p.beckerman at stir.ac.uk  Tue Apr  2 16:53:14 2002
From: a.p.beckerman at stir.ac.uk (Andrew Beckerman)
Date: Tue, 02 Apr 2002 17:53:14 +0100
Subject: simple table of variances
In-Reply-To: <00d401c1da63$cedd4670$6f48110a@THEROCK>
References: <00d401c1da63$cedd4670$6f48110a@THEROCK>
Message-ID: <5.1.0.14.0.20020402174807.00aabc10@falloch.stir.ac.uk>

Elaine - try using summarize() from Frank Harrells HMISC library - 
something like this:

library(hmisc,T) #attach library

attach(your.data) #name of your data frame with columns called "col a" and 
"col b"

summarize(col b, llist(col a), function(x) var(x))

I think that should produce a table for you....

cheers
andrew

