Rod Ball notes:

> The bug in qf() is a known bug in Splus and will be fixed in version 6.1
> (see below). I searched S news and could find no reference to this.
> Barney Campbell the Splus distributor in New Zealand has verified its
> existence since (at least) Splus 3.4.

Based on Knuesel's work, I noted bugs in dt() and dchisq()
in Splus 4.0 on page 158 of "Assessing the Reliability of 
Statistical Software: Part II", The American Statistician, May 1999,
pp. 149-159 (Knuesel's work can be found at 
www.stat.uni-muenchen.de/~knuesel)

Similar errors exist in S-Plus 6.0 for Linux.

e.g.,
                      exact value    S4.0/Windows  
dt(-9.9,100)   8.2022E-17    5.1115E-17     
dt(-10,100)   4.9508E-17     5.1115E-17     

dchisq(2E14,2E14)  0.500      0.5903            

Inquiring minds might wish to test these
values on their current version of S-Plus.

I really never thought these errors would still be around
in 2002, i.e., I never thought it would be necessary to
duplicate Knuesel's work every time there is a new
release.  But apparently it is necessary.
Therefore,  I second Rod Ball's question:

> I would like to know: why isn't there a list of bugs, and fixes as
> Redhat Linux or Microsoft provide?

Bruce

