Subject: Summary and question: summary.aov and contrasts
Message-ID: <3.0.6.32.20020405144715.007a08d0@shaker.med.umn.edu>

My original was about computing and testing contrats with
summary.aov when the design was not balanced.

Thanks to Brian Ripley for indicating that:

> ... the algorithm used by summary.aov assumes order-independence
>(and hence balance) when considering splits.

I am now trying to develop a function that would compute and test
all contrasts for unbalanced designs. I would like some function 
that automatically test all default contrasts for a given factor. 
Does such a function already exist?

Below, I use se.contrast below which works for the simple unbalanced design 
but I don't know yet how to deal with interactions and other more 
complicated design. 

Any help would be appreciated.

Gabriel Baud-Bovy

# unbalanced design
data<-data.frame(tr=rep(1:4,c(7,8,6,8)),
        weight=c(3.52,3.36,3.57,4.19,3.88,3.76,3.94,
                3.47,3.73,3.38,3.87,3.69,3.51,3.35,3.64,
                3.54,3.52,3.61,3.76,3.65,3.51,
                3.74,3.83,3.87,4.08,4.31,3.98,3.86,3.71))

# polynomial contrasts
data$tr<-ordered(data$tr)

# one-way anova
aov.obj<-aov(weight~tr,data,qr=T)
# means and size of each group
means<-tapply(data$weight,data$tr,mean)
nobs<-as.vector(table(data$tr))
# compute estimates for all contrasts
estimates<-means%*%contrasts(data$tr)
# compute sum of squares for all contrasts
ss<-colSums(contrasts(data$tr)*means)^2/
        colSums(contrasts(data$tr)^2/nobs)
# compute standard error for all contrasts
cont <-sapply(levels(data$tr),function(level)data$tr==level)
cont <- cont %*%(contrasts(data$tr)/nobs)
se.cont<-se.contrast(aov.obj,contrast=cont,data=NULL)
# t.test
q<-estimates/se.cont
df<-sum(nobs)-length(nobs)
Pval<-1-pf(q^2,1,df)
#
res<cbind(ss,as.vector(estimates),as.vector(se.cont),as.vector(q),
        rep(df,length(nobs)-1),Pval)
dimnames(res)<-list(dimnames(se.cont)[[2]], 
        c("SS","Estimates","StdError","t","resid.df","P"))

# results (checked with SPSS)
>res
            SS  Estimates   StdError         t resid.df           P 
.L 0.111405921 0.12269092 0.07477106 1.6408878       25 0.113343664
.Q 0.428906408 0.24494048 0.07607720 3.2196304       25 0.003541287
.C 0.005127028 0.02723211 0.07736130 0.3520121       25 0.727779183
# F ratio
>res[, "t"]^2
       .L       .Q        .C 
 2.692513 10.36602 0.1239125
# note that summary.aov does not give the same results
>summary(aov.obj,split=list(tr=list(L=1,Q=2,C=3)))
