1.

You might look into using Frank Harrell's library Hmisc which is included
as a library in SPlus 2000 and SPlus 6 (you do not mention which version
you are using or the platform).
Frank's library provides xYplot which is an enhancement to the standard
trellis function xyplot.
xYplot includes the option to plot error bars.
Good luck!
Madeline

-------------------------------------------------------------------
2.

error.bar accepts the xlim= argument, which you can use to set the range of
x in your picture. So, for example,

error.bar (c(1, 2), c(5, 10), c(2, 2), incr=T) # produces a picture with
bars too spread out
error.bar (c(1, 2), c(5, 10), c(2, 2), incr=T, xlim = c(0, 3)) # looks
better

I hope this helps,
Sam Buttrey

