> Dr Harrell, I understand your point on df. So basically I need to start at 
> or at least close to my df limit from the beginning. Does that include all 
> terms of each variable, though?

Yes, with the exception of pre-testing with pooled tests (e.g., all 
nonlinearities in the model from all predictors combined) that have huge 
P-values.  

> For example, if I have a construction like this:
> 
> mabe1stepb <- step.gam(mabe1glm, scope = list(
> "GeoNutrients" = ~ 1 + poly(GeoNutrients) + poly(GeoNutrients,2),
