On Wed, 17 Apr 2002, Vumani Dlamini wrote:

> I am trying to write a prototype GAM logit program, to aid me understand the
> "backfit" algorithm. The program is given below, but it does not converge
> whilst the one included with S-Plus does, and not sure where I go wrong.

Suppose Y.old was numerically 0 or 1. Then your Z.i gets to include NaNs.
When I ran this, it was Y.new that gave problems, because

R> range(Y.old)
[1] 6.095997e-16 1.000000e+00
R> range(Z.new)
[1]  -318.9338  2975.7233

You need to take a closer look at unclass(binomial()).  glm is not using
the same unprotected formulae that you are.

Backfitting and additive models are not an issue unless X is 2 or more
dimensional.  You are not doing backfitting here, nor fitting an additive
model.  Also, look at your data: much of the range of X has the
probability nearly zero or nearly one.

