From rayharaf at rogers.com  Thu Apr 18 13:49:33 2002
From: rayharaf at rogers.com (Ray Haraf)
Date: Thu, 18 Apr 2002 09:49:33 -0400
Subject: What's wrong with my table() function? -SUMMARY-
Message-ID: <003801c1e6df$dfe35e40$cf867018@bloor.phub.net.cable.rogers.com>

Hello Folks,

 

As usual, replies to my query are 
numerous, kind and helpful. Thanks to Samuel Buttrey, Charles C. Berry, Nick 
Ellis, Stephen Kaluzny, James Holtman, Bill Dunlap, Eric Elguero, Gerrit 
Eichner, Brian D. Ripley, Bert Gunter, and Bob Byers.

What's wrong with my table() 
function? NOTHING! It is my coding of the row variable which is uncorrect. I 
paid attention to cardinality i.e. length of the row variable but not to the 
order of crossing with column, layer and stratum variables. 
