a few other comments:

Typically one should discover differentially expressed genes or at least
some subset of genes first, before clustering on samples or genes. This can
be done in a variety of ways, being careful to control for false postives
(and false negatives).

If you are clustering on genes (BR:variables) and not samples (BR:points)
using a windows pc you should make sure you have your virtual memory set
high. I have the paging file size set to 768-2304 Mb on my laptop for
example. You should also make sure you are using the latest version of
S-PLUS. 

Also, for those interested in large k-means problems, Insightful Miner has a
k-means procedure for handling very large problems based on a paper by
Farnstrom et al (2000). This is inherently scaleable and has been run on
some very large problems (eg many millions of rows).

Michael

