Nick's message:

As your data are ragged, you need to do some special
inputting. 
read.table
won't cope with ragged data. The flush option of scan
ignores anything
beyond the 5th field in this example. To convert to
dates/times look at 
the
functon timeDate.
>
as.data.frame(scan("clipboard",what=list("","",0,0,0),skip=1,flush=T))
